G1921.def:
ἐπι-γινώσκω 
[in LXX chiefly for נָכַר: hi., also for יָדַע, etc. ;] 
"directive" of γινώσκω (AR, Eph., 249), as in cl.; 
__1. to observe, perceive, discern, recognize; 
__(a) absol.: Actes 25:10, 1 Corinthiens 13:12; before ὅτι, Luc 1:22; τ. πνεύματι, before ὅτι, Marc 2:8; 
__(b) with accusative of thing(s): Luc 1:4 5:22, Actes 12:14 27:39, Romains 1:32, 2 Corinthiens 1:13, Colossiens 1:6, 1 Timothée 4:3; ἐν ἐαυτῷ, Marc 5:30; before ὅτι, 1 Corinthiens 14:37; 
__(with) with accusative of person(s): Matthieu 11:27 14:36 17:12, Marc 6:33 (T, αὐτούς, but LTr., WH, R, omit the prop., and LTr., WH, txt., read ἔγνωσαν), Marc 6:54 Luc 24:16, 31, 1 Corinthiens 16:18, 2 Corinthiens 1:14; before ἀπό, with genitive of thing(s), Matthieu 7:16, 20; before ὅτι, Actes 3:10 4:13, 2 Corinthiens 13:5; pass., 1 Corinthiens 13:12; opposite to ἀγνοούμενοι, 2 Corinthiens 6:9. 
__2. to discover, ascertain, determine: Actes 9:30; before ὅτι, Luc 7:37 23:7, Actes 19:34 22:29 24:11 28:1; with accusative of thing(s), before quæst., Actes 23:28; δι᾽ ἣν αἰτίαν, Actes 22:24; παρά, with genitive of person(s), before περ, with genitive of thing(s), Actes 24:8; τ. ὁδὸν τῆς δικαιοσύνης, 2 Pierre 2:21 (cf. Lft., Col., 136; Cremer, 159; M, Pr., 113; AR, Eph., 248 ff.).†

G1980.def:
ἐπι-σκέπτομαι
(late form of ἐπισκοπέω, which see), [in LXX very freq., chiefly for פָּקַד ;] 
__1. to inspect, examine. 
__2. (a) to visit: with accusative, Actes 7:23 15:36 (cf. Juges 15:1); especially, the sick and afflicted (as in MGr. and sometimes in cl.), Matthieu 25:36, 43, Jacques 1:27 (cf. Sir.7:35); 
__(b) in LXX and NT (as פָּקַד in Genèse 21:1, Exode 4:31, Psaumes 8:5, al.), to visit with help, to care for: Luc 1:68, 78 7:16, Actes 15:14, Hébreux 2:6; 
__(with) to visit with punishment (Jérémie 9:25, Psaumes 89:33, al.; cf. MM, Exp., xiv; Cremer, 863).†
